#### Variation 3: Azure Application Gateway with Static Backend Pool (No Dynamic Discovery)

**Use Case**: Web applications (SPAs, traditional web apps) calling services with predictable scaling, low instance churn.

**Architecture**:

- **Router**: Azure Application Gateway (WAF-enabled)
- **Service Registry**: None (static configuration or semi-static updates via Azure Function)
- **Integration**: Application Gateway backend pool manually configured with IP addresses or FQDNs; updated via ARM template, Terraform, or Azure Function polling infrastructure
- **Discovery Mechanism**: Periodic polling (e.g., Azure Function runs every 5 minutes) queries AKS API for pod IPs, updates Application Gateway backend pool via ARM API
- **Health Checking**: Application Gateway active HTTP health probes every 30 seconds; removes unhealthy backends from pool
- **Load Balancing**: Application Gateway round-robin or cookie-based session affinity

**Configuration Example (ARM Template)**:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways",
      "apiVersion": "2021-05-01",
      "name": "appgw-prod",
      "location": "eastus",
      "properties": {
        "sku": {
          "name": "WAF_v2",
          "tier": "WAF_v2",
          "capacity": 2
        },
        "backendAddressPools": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-service-pool",
            "properties": {
              "backendAddresses": [
                {"ipAddress": "10.42.3.5"},
                {"ipAddress": "10.42.3.7"},
                {"ipAddress": "10.42.3.9"},
                {"ipAddress": "10.42.3.12"}
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "backendHttpSettingsCollection": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-http-settings",
            "properties": {
              "port": 8080,
              "protocol": "Http",
              "cookieBasedAffinity": "Enabled",
              "requestTimeout": 30,
              "probe": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/probes', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-health-probe')]"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "probes": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-health-probe",
            "properties": {
              "protocol": "Http",
              "path": "/actuator/health",
              "interval": 30,
              "timeout": 10,
              "unhealthyThreshold": 3,
              "pickHostNameFromBackendHttpSettings": false,
              "minServers": 0,
              "match": {
                "statusCodes": ["200-399"]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "httpListeners": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-listener",
            "properties": {
              "frontendIPConfiguration": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/frontendIPConfigurations', 'appgw-prod', 'frontend-ip')]"
              },
              "frontendPort": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/frontendPorts', 'appgw-prod', 'port-443')]"
              },
              "protocol": "Https",
              "sslCertificate": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/sslCertificates', 'appgw-prod', 'ssl-cert')]"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestRoutingRules": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-routing-rule",
            "properties": {
              "ruleType": "PathBasedRouting",
              "httpListener": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/httpListeners', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-listener')]"
              },
              "urlPathMap": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/urlPathMaps', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-path-map')]"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "urlPathMaps": [
          {
            "name": "pharmacy-path-map",
            "properties": {
              "defaultBackendAddressPool": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/backendAddressPools', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-service-pool')]"
              },
              "defaultBackendHttpSettings": {
                "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/backendHttpSettingsCollection', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-http-settings')]"
              },
              "pathRules": [
                {
                  "name": "pharmacy-api",
                  "properties": {
                    "paths": ["/api/pharmacy/*"],
                    "backendAddressPool": {
                      "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/backendAddressPools', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-service-pool')]"
                    },
                    "backendHttpSettings": {
                      "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways/backendHttpSettingsCollection', 'appgw-prod', 'pharmacy-http-settings')]"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Azure Function for Dynamic Backend Updates (C#)**:

```csharp
// Azure Function: Polls K8s API, Updates App Gateway Backend Pool
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using k8s;
using k8s.Models;
using Microsoft.Azure.Management.Network;
using Microsoft.Azure.Management.Network.Models;
using Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

public static class UpdateAppGatewayBackends
{
    [FunctionName("UpdatePharmacyBackends")]
    public static async Task Run(
        [TimerTrigger("0 */5 * * * *")] TimerInfo timer, // Every 5 minutes
        ILogger log)
    {
        log.LogInformation($"Backend update started at {DateTime.UtcNow}");

        // Connect to Kubernetes API
        var k8sConfig = KubernetesClientConfiguration.InClusterConfig();
        var k8sClient = new Kubernetes(k8sConfig);

        // Get Pharmacy Service Endpoints
        var endpoints = await k8sClient.ListNamespacedEndpointsAsync(
            namespaceParameter: "prod-pharmacy",
            fieldSelector: "metadata.name=pharmacy-service"
        );

        var podIPs = endpoints.Items
            .SelectMany(ep => ep.Subsets)
            .SelectMany(subset => subset.Addresses)
            .Select(addr => addr.Ip)
            .Distinct()
            .ToList();

        log.LogInformation($"Found {podIPs.Count} pharmacy service pods: {string.Join(\", \", podIPs)}");

        // Connect to Azure Resource Management API
        var azureCredentials = SdkContext.AzureCredentialsFactory
            .FromServicePrincipal(
                clientId: Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("AZURE_CLIENT_ID\"),
                clientSecret: Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET\"),
                tenantId: Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"AZURE_TENANT_ID\"),
                environment: AzureEnvironment.AzureGlobalCloud
            );

        var networkClient = new NetworkManagementClient(azureCredentials)
        {
            SubscriptionId = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID")
        };

        // Get Current Application Gateway Configuration
        var appGateway = await networkClient.ApplicationGateways.GetAsync(
            resourceGroupName: "rg-prod-networking",
            applicationGatewayName: "appgw-prod"
        );

        // Update Backend Pool with Current Pod IPs
        var backendPool = appGateway.BackendAddressPools
            .FirstOrDefault(pool => pool.Name == "pharmacy-service-pool");

        if (backendPool != null)
        {
            var newBackends = podIPs.Select(ip => new ApplicationGatewayBackendAddress
            {
                IpAddress = ip
            }).ToList();

            // Check if update needed
            var currentIPs = backendPool.BackendAddresses.Select(b => b.IpAddress).OrderBy(ip => ip);
            var newIPs = newBackends.Select(b => b.IpAddress).OrderBy(ip => ip);

            if (!currentIPs.SequenceEqual(newIPs))
            {
                log.LogInformation("Backend IPs changed, updating Application Gateway...");
                backendPool.BackendAddresses = newBackends;

                await networkClient.ApplicationGateways.CreateOrUpdateAsync(
                    resourceGroupName: "rg-prod-networking",
                    applicationGatewayName: "appgw-prod",
                    parameters: appGateway
                );

                log.LogInformation("Application Gateway backend pool updated successfully");
            }
            else
            {
                log.LogInformation("Backend IPs unchanged, no update needed");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:

- Azure Application Gateway provides WAF, TLS termination, layer 7 routing
- No dependency on external service registry (Eureka, Consul)
- Active health probes ensure traffic to healthy backends only
- Suitable for services with infrequent scaling (updated every 5 minutes acceptable)

**When to Use**: Web applications with WAF requirements, services with predictable instance counts, acceptable 5-minute lag for backend updates, simplified architecture without service registry.
